WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.429 --> 00:00:03.300
Speaker 1: In many ways, the stock market
is not the economy.

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:05.419
We've talked about that endlessly over the
years.

00:00:05.419 --> 00:00:08.340
The stock market tells you one very specific
thing.

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:10.950
It relates to a few other aspects of the economy.

00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:15.840
But stocks can do well while things can be
not so good for much of the American people.

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:21.420
Now, that being said, Donald Trump and many
of his followers hung their hats there, maggots

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:23.130
on stock market performance.

00:00:23.130 --> 00:00:28.670
And more than that, Donald Trump told us if
Joe Biden wins, the stock market will collapse,

00:00:28.670 --> 00:00:29.670
401.

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:31.390
KS would be worth nothing.

00:00:31.390 --> 00:00:35.790
We never believed it in advance because the
stock market generally does better during

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:38.770
Democratic presidents than Republican presidents.

00:00:38.770 --> 00:00:44.360
But now we know it didn't happen because the
stock market has done better during Joe Biden's

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:52.300
first 100 days than during any president's
first hundred days in the last seventy five

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:53.329
years.

00:00:53.329 --> 00:00:57.770
Remember when Trump said this,
Speaker 2: the stock market had to talk about,

00:00:57.770 --> 00:01:01.300
if I'm elected, if he's elected, the stock
Speaker 1: market will crash?

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:02.879
Well, it didn't happen.

00:01:02.879 --> 00:01:09.180
Going back to World War two, the S&amp;P 500,
the broadest of the major three indices, posted

00:01:09.180 --> 00:01:14.190
a better return during Joe Biden's first hundred
days than during any other president dating

00:01:14.190 --> 00:01:15.869
back seventy five years.

00:01:15.869 --> 00:01:21.659
The S&amp;P 500 is up twenty five percent since
Joe Biden was inaugurated.

00:01:21.659 --> 00:01:26.160
It was up under 15 percent under Donald Trump
during the same period.

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:31.150
Previously, the record for the 100 day mark
was 20 percent under John F. Kennedy.

00:01:31.150 --> 00:01:36.509
Now, of course, you will hear from those who
don't want to accept this, that this is only

00:01:36.509 --> 00:01:40.510
because Joe Biden was handed a perfectly timed
covid recovery.

00:01:40.510 --> 00:01:41.520
But that's wrong.

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:46.630
The stock market recovery to pre covid levels
was complete before Trump left office.

00:01:46.630 --> 00:01:48.549
That's not what is going on.

00:01:48.549 --> 00:01:54.020
You will hear well, it's because of the so-called
money printing that the covid stimulus that

00:01:54.020 --> 00:01:56.760
Joe Biden's covid stimulus did know.

00:01:56.760 --> 00:02:02.230
That was relatively recent and that has an
impact that takes time to be seen and understood.

00:02:02.230 --> 00:02:06.869
And, of course, you will also hear from right
wingers saying, well, things might look good

00:02:06.869 --> 00:02:12.849
now, but wait until Joe Biden jacks up the
corporate tax rate and the capital gains rate

00:02:12.849 --> 00:02:15.739
and the income tax rate and then things are
going to implode.

00:02:15.739 --> 00:02:16.779
Probably not.

00:02:16.779 --> 00:02:23.159
Analysts at JPMorgan have looked at the proposal
and have said that it should really be a modest

00:02:23.159 --> 00:02:24.349
impact.

00:02:24.349 --> 00:02:29.800
So to refresh, the stock market is not the
economy, but when one side says basically

00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:34.439
it is and it will crash under Biden and the
opposite happens.

00:02:34.439 --> 00:02:40.029
That's very much worth doing a reality check
on, here's more context on that Trump quote

00:02:40.029 --> 00:02:42.150
about the stock market from earlier day.

00:02:42.150 --> 00:02:45.329
Speaker 2: And Mr. President, I move on to
the next question.

00:02:45.329 --> 00:02:50.180
They say the stock market will talk about
if I'm elected, if he's elected, the stock

00:02:50.180 --> 00:02:51.249
market will crash.

00:02:51.249 --> 00:02:54.650
OK, let me just say very quickly.

00:02:54.650 --> 00:03:00.079
Speaker 3: The idea that the stock market
is booming is his only measure of what's happening

00:03:00.079 --> 00:03:04.340
where I come from in Scranton and Claymont,
that people don't live off of the stock market.

00:03:04.340 --> 00:03:10.469
Just in just the last three or three years
during this crisis, the billionaires in this

00:03:10.469 --> 00:03:17.379
country made, according to the Wall Street,
700 billion more dollars, 700 billion more

00:03:17.379 --> 00:03:20.810
dollars, because that's his only measure.

00:03:20.810 --> 00:03:23.089
What happens to the ordinary people out there?

00:03:23.089 --> 00:03:24.569
Speaker 4: What happens to them?

00:03:24.569 --> 00:03:30.870
Speaker 1: So the point is Joe Biden has not
been hanging his hat on stock market performance.

00:03:30.870 --> 00:03:35.019
That's likely why Joe Biden hasn't been bragging
about it on Twitter.

00:03:35.019 --> 00:03:40.419
Trump did hang his hat on stock market performance
and was completely and totally wrong on what

00:03:40.419 --> 00:03:41.599
would happen.

00:03:41.599 --> 00:03:47.919
And Joe Biden's first 100 day performance
is significantly better, about two thirds

00:03:47.919 --> 00:03:50.370
better than Donald Trump.

00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:53.780
That's not an error, 25 percent versus 15
percent.

00:03:53.780 --> 00:03:57.849
That is 67 percent better under Joe Biden.

00:03:57.849 --> 00:03:59.150
So don't fall for it.

00:03:59.150 --> 00:04:03.010
Yes, they'll have some talking point to try
to talk their way out of it.

00:04:03.010 --> 00:04:06.629
But just follow the data and look at history
as well.

00:04:06.629 --> 00:04:07.659
Let me know your thoughts.

00:04:07.659 --> 00:04:11.370
Did you ever believe the stock market was
going to crash under Joe Biden?

00:04:11.370 --> 00:04:12.639
You can find me on Twitter at David Pakman.

00:04:12.639 --> 00:04:12.799
Let me know

